<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: New Ireland half-yr pretax profit falls.</title>
<headline>New Ireland half-yr pretax profit falls.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>					  (million punts unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		26.7		   vs 27.7</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 4.67		   vs 4.24</p>
<p> Pretax profit	    4.96		   vs 5.29</p>
<p>NOTE - French banking group UAP International holds a majority stake in New Ireland Holdings Plc, an Irish-based insurance group.  </p>
<p> Tax charge		 1.94		   vs 2.00</p>
<p> Attributable	     2.88		   vs 2.98</p>
<p> Record date		October 8</p>
<p> Pay date		   October 16</p>
<p> Ex-dividend date	 September 30</p>
<p>NOTE - New Ireland said it believed the full-year perfomance of the company would be &quot;satisfactory&quot;.</p>
<p>&quot;The group has had a satisfactory performance in the first half of 1996 in a very competitive trading environment,&quot; Managing Director John Casey said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;New Ireland Assurance has again enjoyed substantial growth in recurring life and pensions business and Irish National's performance was satisfactory in a market which, though difficult, is showing some signs that private motor rates are on the increase,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 660 3377</p>
</text>
